// The type of a call that no input file defines.
//
// The native seam types every link-time entry point `int` -- gfx.h says so,
// and idc.py's gen_call returns "int" for exactly this case. Saying it here
// too is what lets `"" + gfx_width()` build the string it looks like it
// builds: without it the type pass has no answer, declines to guess (which is
// the right instinct everywhere else), and the emitter hands a raw int to
// id_concat where a char* belongs.
//
// Only under --extern-ok. With no backend attached an unresolved name is a
// typo, already reported, and inventing a type for it would be inventing a
// meaning for a mistake.
extern_type(string t) {
  string s = t;
  if(t == "" && extern_ok() == 1) {
    s = "int";
  }
} return string s;
